## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time handling of dynamic policies, data privacy, and end-to-end guarantees in KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic per-tenant policy loading from a KCNA topic
- Real-time cache updates with atomic policy changes
- Data redaction strategies (none, partial, full)
- Idempotent sinks and at-least-once guarantees
- Testing under policy updates and message reordering

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(customer, level) {
  if (level === 'full') return { name: null, email: null, card: null };
  if (level === 'partial') {
    const maskedCard = customer.card.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
    const maskedEmail = customer.email.replace(/([^@]{1,2})[^@]*(@.*)/, (m, p1, p2) => p1[0] + '**' + p2);
    return { ...customer, card: maskedCard, email: maskedEmail };
  }
  return customer;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests encryption design, tenancy isolation, rotation semantics, cross-region distribution, and auditability in KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption with per-tenant KEK and DEK
- KMS integration, key-versioning, and cross-region propagation
- Zero-downtime rotation and background re-wrapping
- Audit trails and RBAC for keys

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: envelope encrypt a payload
function encryptPayload(plaintext, tenantId, kmsClient) {
  const DEK = kmsClient.getDataKey(tenantId);
  const wrappedDEK = kmsClient.wrapKey(DEK, tenantId);
  const ciphertext = cryptoAesGCM(nonce, DEK, plaintext);
  return { ciphertext, wrappedDEK, keyVersion: kmsClient.currentVersion(tenantId) };
}

function decryptPayload(payloadPkg, tenantId, kmsClient) {
  const DEK = kmsClient.unwrapKey(payloadPkg.wrappedDEK, tenantId);
  return cryptoAesGCMDecrypt(payloadPkg.ciphertext, DEK);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the zero-downtime rotation in production, including canaries and rollback?
- What metrics and alerts would you add to detect rotation-related failures and data-inaccessibility?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes KCNA security design, tenant isolation, and practical key management choices under constraints like rotation and revocation.

## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption with per-tenant DEKs
- Hierarchical KMS/HSM wrapping and rotation
- Per-tenant access checks and audit proofs
- Rollout/rollback with minimal downtime and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for envelope encryption
function encryptEvent(event, tenantId, kms, store) {
  const dek = store.getDEK(tenantId);
  const ciphertext = aesGcmEncrypt(event.payload, dek);
  return { ciphertext, headers: { tenantId, keyId: dek.id, epoch: dek.epoch } };
}
function decryptEvent(record, store) {
  const dek = store.getDEK(record.headers.tenantId, record.headers.keyId);
  return aesGcmDecrypt(record.ciphertext, dek);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rotation can be performed with zero downtime?
- How would you handle compromised KEKs and re-encryption scope?
